<title>PORTUGAL: Bank/Portugal says no forex, money markets Dec 2.</title>
<headline>Bank/Portugal says no forex, money markets Dec 2.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Portugal (BP) announced that the Portuguese foreign exchange and money markets will be closed on Monday because of the Organisation for Security and Cooperation in Europe (OSCE) summit in Lisbon.</p>
<p>But it said December 2 would remain the valid date of expiry on existing contracts.</p>
<p>The government has declared Monday, December 2 a public holiday, and the Lisbon bourse already said it would close.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3113121</p>
</text>
